      <h1><span class="accent">Picture Converter</span> for Chrome</h1>
      <p class="hero-copy">
        Save the website image you actually need in the format you need. Or open a local WebP, HEIC, AVIF or SVG and convert it without another converter tab.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="install" href="https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/image-converter/ooiklbnjmhbcfnllkgjahadblibecgfj?utm_source=layerporter&utm_medium=website&utm_campaign=picture-converter-landing&utm_content=hero" rel="noopener">
          Add Picture Converter to Chrome <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
        <div class="micro">One selected web image or one local file at a time. Multi-file processing is available for PDF.</div>
      </div>
      <ul class="proofline" aria-label="Common conversions">
        <li>WebP → JPG</li>
        <li>HEIC → JPG</li>
        <li>SVG → PNG</li>
        <li>PNG → ICO</li>
        <li>Images → PDF</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="local-line"><strong>Processed locally.</strong> Nothing is uploaded for conversion.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="product-proof" aria-label="Picture Converter interface preview">
      <div class="browser">
        <div class="browser-top">
          <div class="dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
          <div class="address">example.com/product-image.webp</div>
          <div class="ext-icon">⇄</div>
        </div>
        <div class="browser-body">
          <div class="web-page">
            <div class="web-toolbar"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
            <div class="photo-stage">
              <div class="selected-photo"><div class="pick-ring"></div></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="panel">
            <div class="panel-head">
              <div class="panel-brand"><strong>Picture Converter</strong><span>LOCAL</span></div>
              <div class="mode"><span class="active">From page</span><span>From computer</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="file-preview">
              <div class="thumb"></div>
              <div><b>product-image.webp</b><small>WEBP · selected from website</small></div>
            </div>
            <div class="output">
              <div class="output-label"><span>Output format</span><span>Recommended</span></div>
              <div class="formats">
                <div class="format">PNG</div>
                <div class="format active">JPG</div>
                <div class="format">WEBP</div>
                <div class="format">PDF</div>
                <div class="format">ICO</div>
              </div>
              <div class="quality">
                <div class="quality-row"><span>Quality</span><span>82%</span></div>
                <div class="track"></div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="panel-bottom">
              <div class="download-btn"><span>Download JPG</span><span>↓</span></div>
              <div class="local-proof">Processed locally · files stay on your device</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="float-proof"><i>⇄</i><div><strong>One image. Right format.</strong><small>Website or local file</small></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap">
    <div class="task-strip">
      <div><b>WEB IMAGE</b><small>Pick one image from the current page</small></div>
      <div><b>LOCAL FILE</b><small>Convert WebP, HEIC, AVIF, SVG and more</small></div>
      <div><b>PDF</b><small>Combine up to 30 images in page order</small></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section" id="web">
    <div class="section-number">01 · FROM WEBSITE</div>
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>Save the image. Skip the converter detour.</h2>
      <p>When a site gives you WebP but the next app wants JPG or PNG, select the picture once and save the converted copy from the same browser workflow.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="web-flow">
      <div class="web-flow-visual">
        <div class="site-card">
          <div class="site-card-top"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
          <div class="site-image"><div class="convert-pill">Convert image ⇄</div></div>
          <div class="site-result"><span>PNG</span><span class="active">JPG</span><span>WEBP</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="section-copy">
        <span class="num">WEB · ONE SELECTED IMAGE</span>
        <h3>Choose only what you need.</h3>
        <p>Picture Converter works with the single page image you select instead of collecting every graphic from the website.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Right-click workflow <span>Convert Image</span></li>
          <li>Keyboard shortcut <span>Alt + Shift + C</span></li>
          <li>Output <span>JPG · PNG · WebP · PDF · ICO</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="dark">
    <section class="wrap section" id="local">
      <div class="section-number">02 · LOCAL FILES</div>
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>One Picture Converter. Two everyday jobs.</h2>
        <p>Use the same extension when the image is already on your computer. Open it, choose the destination format, adjust quality when needed, and save the new copy.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="local-shell">
        <div class="local-copy">
          <span>LOCAL · FORMAT CHANGE</span>
          <h3>WebP and HEIC stop being a compatibility problem.</h3>
          <p>Modern web formats and phone photos become files your editor, upload form or desktop app can actually accept.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="local-ui">
          <div class="local-ui-top"><strong>From computer</strong><span>Local processing</span></div>
          <div class="drop">
            <div class="drop-icon">+</div>
            <b>Choose an image</b>
            <small>or drag & drop it here</small>
            <div class="input-row">
              <span>PNG</span><span>JPG</span><span>WEBP</span><span>HEIC</span><span>AVIF</span><span>SVG</span><span>JFIF</span><span>BMP</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="convert-flow">
            <div class="file-card"><b>IMG_1842.HEIC</b><small>iPhone photo · source</small></div>
            <div class="arrow">→</div>
            <div class="file-card output-card"><b>IMG_1842.JPG</b><small>Broad compatibility · output</small></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <section class="wrap pdf-section" id="pdf">
    <div class="pdf-grid">
      <div class="pdf-copy">
        <div class="section-number">03 · IMAGES TO PDF</div>
        <h2>30 images. One ordered PDF.</h2>
        <p>Add one photo or up to 30 images, arrange the page order, remove what you do not need, then download one document. Multi-file processing is deliberately limited to this workflow.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pdf-demo" aria-label="Images to PDF preview">
        <div class="pdf-top"><strong>4 images → one PDF</strong><span>Drag or reorder pages</span></div>
        <div class="pages">
          <div class="page-thumb"><span class="page-num">1</span></div>
          <div class="page-thumb"><span class="page-num">2</span></div>
          <div class="page-thumb"><span class="page-num">3</span></div>
          <div class="page-thumb"><span class="page-num">4</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="pdf-footer"><span>4 pages ready</span><div class="pdf-button">Download PDF · 4 pages ↓</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap format-section">
    <div class="section-number">04 · OUTPUTS</div>
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>Choose for the next app, not the current file.</h2>
      <p>The point is not to “convert an image.” The point is to end up with the format your editor, website, upload form, document or favicon slot expects.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="format-grid">
      <div class="format-card"><b>JPG</b><small>Compatibility</small><p>For photos, forms and apps that expect a broadly supported image file.</p></div>
      <div class="format-card"><b>PNG</b><small>Transparency</small><p>For graphics, editing and sources where transparency needs to be preserved.</p></div>
      <div class="format-card"><b>WebP</b><small>For the web</small><p>For a modern web image with adjustable output quality.</p></div>
      <div class="format-card"><b>PDF</b><small>Document</small><p>For one image or an ordered document made from up to 30 images.</p></div>
      <div class="format-card"><b>ICO</b><small>Favicon</small><p>For turning an existing graphic into an icon file for browser and desktop use.</p></div>
    </div>
    <div class="signal" aria-label="Common format conversions">
      <span>WebP → JPG</span>
      <span>HEIC → JPG</span>
      <span>AVIF → JPG</span>
      <span>SVG → PNG</span>
      <span>PNG → ICO</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap compare">
    <div class="compare-grid">
      <div>
        <div class="section-number">05 · LESS FRICTION</div>
        <h2>Remove the unnecessary middle website.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="flow-compare">
        <div class="flow-row old">
          <b>Without</b>
          <div><span>Find image</span><i>→</i><span>Download</span><i>→</i><span>Open converter site</span><i>→</i><span>Upload</span><i>→</i><span>Download again</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-row new">
          <b>With extension</b>
          <div><span>Select image</span><i>→</i><span>Choose format</span><i>→</i><span>Save</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap faq" id="faq">
    <div class="faq-grid">
      <div>
        <div class="section-number">06 · FAQ</div>
        <h2>Questions.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <details open>
          <summary><span>01</span>What is Picture Converter?<i>+</i></summary>
          <p>Picture Converter is a Chrome extension for saving one selected website image in another format, converting a local image file, and combining up to 30 images into one PDF.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary><span>02</span>Can I convert WebP to JPG or PNG?<i>+</i></summary>
          <p>Yes. Open a WebP from your computer or select one on a website, then choose JPG or PNG as the output.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary><span>03</span>Can I convert HEIC photos to JPG?<i>+</i></summary>
          <p>Yes. HEIC is supported as an input format and can be converted to JPG or PNG.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary><span>04</span>Can I save an image from a website as JPG or PNG?<i>+</i></summary>
          <p>Yes. Pick one image on the current page, open it in the converter, choose the output format, and save the converted copy.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary><span>05</span>Can several files be processed together?<i>+</i></summary>
          <p>Yes, when they are combined into one PDF. The limit is 30 images and you can change their page order before saving. Other output formats are created one picture at a time.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary><span>06</span>Are files uploaded for conversion?<i>+</i></summary>
          <p>No. Conversion is processed locally in the browser. Local files are opened only when you choose them through the extension.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary><span>07</span>Can I control output quality?<i>+</i></summary>
          <p>Yes. A quality control is available for JPG and WebP output.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="final">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow"><span class="mark">⇄</span> Picture Converter · Chrome</div>
      <h2>Get the format you needed in the first place.</h2>
      <p>From a website image or a local file to JPG, PNG, WebP, PDF or ICO — without adding another converter site to the workflow.</p>
      <a class="install" href="https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/image-converter/ooiklbnjmhbcfnllkgjahadblibecgfj?utm_source=layerporter&utm_medium=website&utm_campaign=picture-converter-landing&utm_content=final" rel="noopener">
        Add Picture Converter to Chrome <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
      <div class="final-meta">WEBP · HEIC · AVIF · SVG · JPG · PNG · PDF · ICO</div>
    </div>
  </section>
